  "notes": "Original label version with marbled Elektra 'butterfly' labels, pressed by [l447694] per stamped 'P' and etched 'CP' in runouts.\n\nLabels are extremely similar to the Terre Haute pressing [r=5675190] and the Monarch pressing [r=5675173].\n\nReleased with a gatefold jacket and printed color paper Elektra Records / Nonesuch Records inner sleeve.\n\nFrom rear cover:\nall selections written by the stooges,\ncopyright © 1970 by paradox music & stooge staffel music BMI\n\nrecorded at elektra sound recorders, los angeles, calif.\n\nElektra Records, 15 Columbus Circle, New York City 10023\n© 1970 by Elektra Records\n\nFrom inner sleeve:\nElektra Records / Nonesuch Records 1855 Broadway, New York, N.Y. 10023\n\nFrom labels:\nElektra Records, 15 Columbus Circle, New York City 10023",
  "released_formatted": "Aug 1970",
